CloudBurrow patch 75 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1601).

The bug: patch 0065 (#1584) looks up the dataset of each table a query
added before the query's transaction commits, through
metaRepo.FindProject, which takes a new connection of its own. Once the
transaction had written rows (a CREATE TABLE AS SELECT of a few thousand
rows, the CloudBurrow front's copy of a table that datasets.delete or
tables.delete keeps for time travel), that connection waited for the
transaction's lock until the request's deadline: every such query took
a minute, and a datasets.delete of a dataset with a loaded table
outlasted the client's context.

The patch reads the project in the query's own transaction
(FindProjectWithConn on tx.Tx(), in metadata mode), as the loader does.

